WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640
Devil's advocacy involves deliberately questioning assumptions and conclusions to identify

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.235
weaknesses in reasoning.

00:00:06.235 --> 00:00:09.680
Red team thinking introduces alternative perspectives that challenge prevailing

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.340
narratives.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.965
These approaches should not create conflict for its own sake.

00:00:12.965 --> 00:00:16.660
Their purpose is improving analytical quality before decisions are made.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.820
Constructive challenge works best when it is focused on the reasoning, evidence,

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.320
and assumptions rather than personal disagreement.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.840
The goal is sharper analysis, not winning an argument.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.805
Used well, devil's advocacy and red team thinking help teams notice blind spots,

00:00:28.805 --> 00:00:31.080
test confidence, and strengthen recommendations.
